{#
    `.. configuration-block::` — the same setting written in two languages.

    The second tab form in the same output format, and it arrives as its own
    markup: a `role="tablist"` of buttons, a panel each, and `display: none` on
    all but the first. The switching is a script the renderer does not ship, so
    left alone it is a row of buttons that do nothing above a block that cannot
    be reached.

    It is the same content as `.. tabs::` and it becomes the same element, for
    the reason that decides every other template here: a reader must not have
    to learn which directive an author reached for. What is dropped is the
    tablist markup — `sds-tabs` builds its own, with the arrow keys — and the
    panel ids, which only that script used.

    One thing this does not yet do is what the directive is for: choosing PHP
    once and having every block on the page follow. That needs the element to
    know about its siblings, and it is written down in `guides-theme/GAPS.md`
    rather than half-built here.
#}
<sds-tabs>
    {%- for tab in node.tabs %}
        <sds-tab-item label="{{ tab.label }}">
            {{- renderNode(tab.content) -}}
        </sds-tab-item>
    {%- endfor %}
</sds-tabs>
